# No em dash (U+2014) in product copy

## Ban

Do not use the Unicode em dash (U+2014) in visitor-facing or maintainer copy:

- `public/data/**` (EN and pt-PT JSON: personal, experience, projects, skills, ui, meta)
- `src/**` user-visible strings (TS/TSX/CSS content, not vendor comments)
- `docs/**` and repo Markdown we edit

Treat an existing em dash as a **punctuation mistake**. **Do not** mechanically replace every `—` with ASCII `-`.

Skip skill packs (`.cursor/skills`, `.agents/skills`, `.claude/skills`): those are upstream.

## Choose the correct replacement

| Role of the (wrong) em dash | Prefer | Portfolio example |
|---|-----|---|
| Name then gloss / stack | colon | `Wisdom: multi-tenant job tracking` |
| Label then detail | colon | `Professional IT: L1/L2/L3 design` |
| Title then subtitle | colon | `# Experience: E2E delivery` |
| Aside / cross-ref | parentheses | `OBS overlays (RTMP/SRT ingest)` |
| Two related clauses | semicolon | `I ship the API; the SPA consumes it.` |
| New thought | period | `This is not a panel. It is a hardened VPS.` |
| Empty / N/A cell | ASCII hyphen alone | `\| - \|` |

ASCII `-` is correct for **hyphenated words** (`full-stack`, `pt-PT`), **CLI flags**, and **numeric ranges** (`1-10`). It is usually **wrong** as a clause separator.

En dash (U+2013) is different. Existing CV periods may keep `June 2010 – Present`. For new ranges, ASCII `2010-Present` is fine.

## Workflow

- When you **edit** a file that still contains U+2014, fix each hit in that file in the same change.
- Do not scrub the whole repo just to burn down em dashes.
- Check: `npm run lint:em-dash` (`scripts/check-no-em-dash.mjs`). Not part of `npm run lint` until copy is clean.
